{"id": "sevt_01Xt8pQ23KhEDCjYCoikNLvq", "content": [{"text": "## Findings\n\n**Timeline**\n- Checkout p99 flat at ~70\u201380ms through 14:21, then jumps to 3404ms at the 14:22 bucket and keeps climbing (5800ms+ by 14:59).\n- Error rate stays <1% the whole time \u2014 this is pure latency, not failures.\n\n**Deploy correlation**\n- `checkout` `6db1b9b` deployed 14:22:30. First per-row query log line appears 14:22:31.103Z. Spike and deploy line up to the second.\n- Cart `50293ce` (14:21:05, \"add exponential backoff\") is a red herring: it's a different service, and adding backoff only adds latency on retries \u2014 not seen here.\n\n**Diff**\n`6db1b9b` \"refactor order summary builder\" replaced a single batched query with a per-row query inside a loop:\n- before: `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=ids)` \u2014 one query, grouped in memory\n- after: `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=order.order_id)` per order in a `for` loop\n\nThis is a classic N+1 regression (top item on the runbook's \"things that have burned us\").\n\n**Log confirmation**\n- Zero `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` lines before 14:22; they start at 14:22:31, immediately post-deploy.\n- ~16 of these queries fire per `request_id` after the deploy \u2014 the N+1 fan-out driving the p99.\n\nFix: revert `6db1b9b` or restore the batched `order_id__in` query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `6db1b9b` \u2014 refactor replaced the batched `OrderItem` query with a per-order query in a loop, causing an N+1 fan-out (~16 queries/request) that blew up checkout p99.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:30:11.481872Z", "type": "agent.message"}
